<h3>About Government Gateway Authentication</h3>
<p>When you click the payment button, you will be redirected to <b>tax.service.gov.uk</b> for identity verification:</p>
<ol>
<li>Enter your Government Gateway ID (or create one using your company details)</li>
<li>Verify your identity through GOV.UK Verify</li>
<li>Enter your bank details for payment</li>
<li>Payment confirmation will be emailed to you</li>
</ol>

<p style="font-size:14px;background:#E8EAF6;padding:12px;border-radius:4px">
<b>Why GOV.UK Verify for penalty payments?</b> HMRC requires identity verification for all payments over £1,000 to prevent fraudulent payments. GOV.UK Verify is the UK government's official identity assurance service. For overseas companies (like yours, registered in China), you may need to provide additional documentation: your company registration certificate, the director's passport, and proof of your UK business address. The offline_access permission maintains your payment session while you gather and upload these documents (typically 10-15 minutes). This is a standard requirement for non-UK resident companies paying UK tax penalties.
</p>

